    "open_questions": [
      "Separate Ways (Frontiers, 1983), his best-known drum part, has a human tab that lines up with the record, but it holds 113 distinct bars, eight of them sextuplet fills, and packs into 30 parts at best; Stone in Love's outro puts a bar of 2/4 after every five of 4/4 and needs 28. More section letters, or a written section that can change grid or meter bar by bar, would let both in unbent.",
      "No human transcription of a Vital Information, Steps Ahead or later fusion record of his is on Songsterr (Vital Information's \"Sacred Treasure\" and Steps Ahead's are machine drafts, and Steps Ahead's Magnetic is Peter Erskine's): his own band's playing is not yet modelled.",
      "Mirage: the tab writes 185 and the record runs at about 189; between bars 97 and 200, where the solos fill the mix, the onset match is unsure, though both ends and the groove at bars 132-142 sit where the tab puts them.",
      "Who's Crying Now: the tab writes a crash with the ride and the snare on 2 in seven bars of the guitar solo; read as the crash taking the right hand. Check the record.",
      "Whether any Frontiers parts used electronic drums: no source read says so; the kit that recorded it is the acoustic Sonor Phonic."
    ]
  },
